Lineage and attribution
================================================================================

This reference architecture descends from two upstream projects. It is a
clean-room rewrite — patterns re-expressed from concept, with generic
placeholders and fictional examples — not a copy of either upstream. Credit is
given here gratefully and explicitly.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. freskhu/genesis  — Apache License 2.0
   https://github.com/freskhu/genesis
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The functional structure of this project — the CEO-virtual orchestration model,
specialised-agent delegation, smart routing, the quality gate, the skills/hooks
layout, and the transactional-store schema conventions — descends from the
`genesis` project by freskhu, who shared the structure with our team privately,
ahead of that project's public release. `genesis` is distributed under the
Apache License 2.0; this project preserves that attribution as required for
derivative works. Where this repository reproduces upstream names or schema
nomenclature (for example the traceability tables `procedural_memory` and
`activity_history`), the reproduction is conscious and attributed, never
accidental.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. MemPalace/mempalace  — MIT License
   https://github.com/MemPalace/mempalace
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The 3-tier memory system and its taxonomy — the notion of a semantic memory
"palace", and the vocabulary of wings / rooms / halls / drawers, mining and
traversal, the diary, and the bitemporal knowledge graph (valid_from /
valid_to) — inherit concepts from the `mempalace` project, which was the
original engine for our memory layer before an internal successor was built.
`mempalace` is distributed under the MIT License, which is compatible with the
Apache License 2.0. This attribution is offered as credit for the concepts and
taxonomy we build upon; where any MIT-licensed source is adapted, its copyright
notice is preserved alongside.

